{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/823219-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-strong-fera","id":823219,"title":"Deadliest supernatural warrior: the strong Fera","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-04T04:20:08-08:00","id":823219,"title":"Deadliest supernatural warrior: the strong Fera","content":"The battle has moved on to the strong Fera: the Gurahl, the Garou, and the Mokol\u00e9.<br /> <br /> Place your bets (and then resolve them immediately by going to: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/799293-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-changers-and-suckers?p=823216#post823216\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...216#post823216</a> ).<br /> <br /> Any guesses on the &quot;mystery guest&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T18:58:11-08:00","id":823933,"title":"","content":"So I read it and one thing that stands out, the idea that the kiss is irresistible to the Fera. I realize the V20 book doesn't get specific on the kiss but the only book I have ever seen that actually gets into the nitty gritty of a crossover between vamps and garou is the Werewolf Storyteller's Handbook. On page 198 it does state that shifterss do not count as mortals for most powers. Then goes right into the kiss as being one such power, and it can be resisted as if they were vampires. Not sure if you want to count this book because it is older, but the older vampire books never covered the effect of the kiss on werewolves either. This is the only book I have seen to cover it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T19:00:09-08:00","id":823937,"title":"","content":"Also...V20 does state that the fangs must pierce skin, couldn't it be argued (especially with a mokole who has scaled armor) that if the vampire does no damage he has not pierced the skin? An example that comes to mind is the Nagah who must do at least 1 pt of dmg (after soak) with a bite attack in order to be able to inject venom, essentially that 1 pt of dmg representing the fang getting past the skin. Curious to what you decide on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T21:59:27-08:00","id":824004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/823219-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-strong-fera?p=823937#post823937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also...V20 does state that the fangs must pierce skin, couldn't it be argued (especially with a mokole who has scaled armor) that if the vampire does no damage he has not pierced the skin? An example that comes to mind is the Nagah who must do at least 1 pt of dmg (after soak) with a bite attack in order to be able to inject venom, essentially that 1 pt of dmg representing the fang getting past the skin. Curious to what you decide on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I brought up that point as well.<br /> <br /> Also, the Archid trait Terrible Claws does not add 3 to claw damage, but increases base claw damage to Str+3. The Mokole also should've taken Shed as its second Gift since it was only assigned 1 gift. Mind you, the fights are incredibly limited in scope and in no way represent how a fight would be run at a table. Once I accepted that fact, this thought exercise became a bit amusing to read.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely surprised at how well the Gurahl performs, but I think that mostly has to do with the wonky clinch mechanics being used. I have never seen a Gurahl actually be able to hold its own against a Garou (of equal rank) generally because extra actions are so overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-05-2016, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:14:13-08:00","id":824010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/823219-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-strong-fera?p=824004#post824004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I brought up that point as well.<br /> <br /> Also, the Archid trait Terrible Claws does not add 3 to claw damage, but increases base claw damage to Str+3. The Mokole also should've taken Shed as its second Gift since it was only assigned 1 gift. Mind you, the fights are incredibly limited in scope and in no way represent how a fight would be run at a table. Once I accepted that fact, this thought exercise became a bit amusing to read.<br /> <br /> I'm genuinely surprised at how well the Gurahl performs, but I think that mostly has to do with the wonky clinch mechanics being used. I have never seen a Gurahl actually be able to hold its own against a Garou (of equal rank) generally because extra actions are so overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Deadly Hugbear is a distinct possibility, able to use Strength to hit and then deal damage as well. Happiness is knowing that no one can beat your 25-dice specialized Brawl roll, or take the damage that you're dealing out.<br /> <br /> (There's a reason that Exalted 3rd edition dispensed with Strength-based targeting)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:10:57-08:00","id":824070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/823219-deadliest-supernatural-warrior-the-strong-fera?p=823937#post823937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also...V20 does state that the fangs must pierce skin, couldn't it be argued (especially with a mokole who has scaled armor) that if the vampire does no damage he has not pierced the skin? An example that comes to mind is the Nagah who must do at least 1 pt of dmg (after soak) with a bite attack in order to be able to inject venom, essentially that 1 pt of dmg representing the fang getting past the skin. Curious to what you decide on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it does seem plausible you could go that way. I'm not going to, on grounds of not wanting to rerun 200ish battles ^_^ in practice, this should only make a major difference for the Mokol\u00e9; the Kiss damage dice pool would typically be 13 or so.<br /> <br /> Currently, everyone resists the Kiss with willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T01:18:44-08:00","id":824100,"title":"","content":"Odd. I was almost sure that I wrote up a post about this last night... Ah well, CeltSPZ and idpersona sorted it already <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T07:27:11-08:00","id":825397,"title":"","content":"I'd want to place my bet on that guest's identity: Nagah! (pretty please ^^). By the way,Cheesefondue, i'd want to thank you about all these posts and the work you've done: they are most funny and informative. Seriously, i don't get why there's so few people following them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_